      <activity id="fffc0a77-3211-5622-9d3b-3e5da9301bcb" activityNameId="79f3bc46-d0bb-5433-a045-36211eafc673" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Kitchen worktop, aluminiumtrihydroxide-acrylic glass, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Kitchen worktop, aluminiumtrihydroxide-acrylic glass, at plant
The electricity demand for cutting and grinding of the worktops is estimated based on electricity consumption of wood processing. Aluminiumtrihydroxide-acrylic glass can be processed similar to hardwood. The processing losses are assumed to be 10%. Input of packaging materials is estimated based on similar kitchen worktops.;
UUID: 28b1b9e6-da8c-3fe3-83be-52cd77261f28
This data set includes the materials needed for the production of kitchen countertops made from aluminiumtrihydroxide-acrylic glass. The kitchen worktop has a thickness of 12 mm. An average kitchen countertop has the measures of 2400 mm x 600 mm (1.44 m2). The sink is not included. Transport is estimated according to the ecoinvent standard distances for Switzerland.
Location: Data valid for Switzerland
Technology: Average production
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: unknown 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_28b1b9e6-da8c-3fe3-83be-52cd77261f28.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
